Package: poolinfo
Type: Package
Title: Reliability-Profile Diagnostics for Partial Pooling
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("JoonHo", "Lee",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
    email = "jlee296@ua.edu",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-4019-8703"))
Description: Summarizes how much a set of estimates with known standard
    errors, such as the site estimates of a multisite trial, the studies of
    a meta-analysis or the direct estimates of small areas, can say about
    the individual units under a normal hierarchical model. Computes the
    site reliabilities and their informativeness, mean reliability,
    dispersion and concentration, with posterior means and intervals from
    numerical integration over the between-site standard deviation, design
    calculations, plots made with 'ggplot2', and tables and sentences for
    reporting. The diagnostics
    follow Lee (2026). Supported by the Institute of Education Sciences
    through Grant R305D240078 to the University of Alabama.
